cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "GooGym2D: A Gymnasium 2D bridge-construction environment"
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software itself and the
  paper describing the work it comes from.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Sun
    given-names: Tao
  - family-names: Wang
    given-names: Shaoyi
  - family-names: Schleicher
    given-names: Simon
  - family-names: Weber
    given-names: Ramon E.
repository-code: "https://github.com/LupoSun/GooGym2D"
url: "https://luposun.github.io/GooGym2D/"
abstract: >-
  A headless Gymnasium environment for incremental 2D bridge construction,
  with graph-state utilities and a lightweight axial truss FEM pipeline for
  terminal structural evaluation. Extracted from the research codebase behind
  the IASS 2026 and ACADIA 2026 papers on learning structural design intuition
  from human demonstrations.
keywords:
  - reinforcement-learning
  - imitation-learning
  - gymnasium
  - structural-design
  - computational-design
  - truss
